/target
.vs/
# .NET's build folders - only where there are C# projects: a Rust crate's
# src/bin holds sources (lib/console/src/bin/match.rs was lost to a
# broader rule here, never committed).
lib/csharp/bin/
lib/csharp/obj/
Examples/Desktop/CSharp/**/bin/
Examples/Desktop/CSharp/**/obj/

# The browser module is a build artefact: Examples/Web/Rust/01-Linked/build.cmd makes it.
Examples/Web/Rust/01-Linked/web/*.wasm

# The DOS build: what a run leaves behind. The programs are tracked - the
# loader .COM files and the flat binaries they load, OWLOS.BIN, HELLO.BIN
# and DEMO.BIN, which Examples/DOS/Rust/build.cmd makes - so that
# DOS_Rust_Demo.cmd runs from a fresh clone without a nightly Rust, as
# OWLOSRES.BIN does below. The screens a run dumps are .BIN too, and are
# named here one by one.
Examples/DOS/Rust/target/
Examples/DOS/Rust/*.LOG
Examples/DOS/Rust/OWLOS.OUT
Examples/DOS/Rust/TRACE.TXT
Examples/DOS/Rust/SHOT.BIN
Examples/DOS/Rust/SCREEN.BIN
Examples/DOS/Rust/AUTOTYPE.TXT
Examples/DOS/Rust/dbx.log

# What a DOS run or build leaves behind, in any of the DOS folders: the
# screens F12 wrote, what RUN.BAT and MAKE.BAT saw, a compiler's leftovers.
# The programs themselves (.COM, .EXE) are tracked, like their sources, so
# a DOS machine can run them without the compilers.
Examples/DOS/*/SHOT.TXT
Examples/DOS/*/SHOTS.TXT
Examples/DOS/*/SHOT.BIN
Examples/DOS/*/RUN.OUT
Examples/DOS/*/MAKE.OUT
Examples/DOS/*/AUTOTYPE.TXT
Examples/DOS/*/TRACE.TXT
Examples/DOS/*/*.OBJ
Examples/DOS/*/*.TPU
# The commander's test plays with files: TEST.CMD makes this folder afresh.
Examples/DOS/Commandr/PLAY/
# CWSDPMI's swap file, left behind wherever DOSBox-X was closed while a
# program was still running - which is how a DOS launcher is ended.
CWSDPMI.SWP

# The resident's Rust build. OWLOSRES.BIN and OWLOSRES.COM, which it
# makes, are tracked: a program in assembler, Pascal or C needs them and
# should not need a nightly Rust to get them.
lib/dos/target/
lib/dos/*.LOG
lib/dos/TRACE.TXT

# The folder the web demo reads and saves (Examples/Web/files): only its
# welcome file is the repository's; what a visitor saves there is theirs.
Examples/Web/files/*
!Examples/Web/files/WELCOME.TXT

# The core for JavaScript: lib/js/build.cmd makes it.
lib/js/owlosui-wire.wasm

# The live demo site, as Examples/Web/site/build.mjs makes it.
_site/

# What the DOS commander leaves for its batch file when it steps out to run
# a program; gone again once the program has run.
Examples/DOS/Commandr/RUNPROG.BAT
Examples/DOS/Commandr/COMMANDR.SAV
